From 81aa300b2507d035ac996ba05e44210ff30dcbb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TeamHarrisCali <34009957+TeamHarrisCali@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:04:26 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 129/131] Memory: smaller kernel reserve, firmware copy freed,
 memreport, capped logs

The card log of the "tar: SIGSEGV" (2026-11-17): "tar: page allocation
failure. order:8", 2.1 MB free, tar needing 868 KB in one piece, and a
free 1 MB block that the reserve check refused (min_free_kbytes 508 KB,
part of it required in large pieces: the check failed at 128 KB).
- rc: min_free_kbytes 192 at boot (the same request then passes).
- dsiwifi: the firmware file's copy (up to 128 KB) is freed once the
  chip runs it, and by "clear"; the Wi-Fi window and the test script
  load the file again before the next ifconfig wlan0 up.
- binfmt_flat: "Unable to allocate RAM for process data, errno 0"
  becomes "<program>: not enough memory in one piece for its data (N
  bytes): out of memory". (The process still dies: the failure comes
  after exec's point of no return, which the shell shows as SIGSEGV.)
- memreport: each process's memory and slack (/proc/PID/status), RAM,
  the kernel's reserve, free blocks by size and the largest one.
- dsnet: /tmp/dsnet.log and /tmp/dsnet-dhcp.log become NAME.old past
  32 KB (/tmp is RAM).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 linux-2.6.x/arch/arm/mach-nds/dsiwifi.c |   7 ++
 linux-2.6.x/fs/binfmt_flat.c            |   4 +-
 user/microwin/src/demos/nanox/dsnet.c   |  21 +++-
 vendors/Nintendo/DSI/memreport.c        | 145 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 vendors/Nintendo/DSI/rc                 |   4 +
 5 files changed, 178 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 vendors/Nintendo/DSI/memreport.c

diff --git a/linux-2.6.x/arch/arm/mach-nds/dsiwifi.c b/linux-2.6.x/arch/arm/mach-nds/dsiwifi.c
index 5412be927..8a82c4dbc 100644
--- a/linux-2.6.x/arch/arm/mach-nds/dsiwifi.c
+++ b/linux-2.6.x/arch/arm/mach-nds/dsiwifi.c
@@ -1225,6 +1225,11 @@ static int w_open(struct net_device *dev)
 	fail_state = 0;
 	conn_at = 0;
 	upload(1);
+	/* the firmware file's copy (up to 128 KB) is not needed once the chip runs it: give it back (memory is tight; the Wi-Fi window
+	 * and the test script load the file again before the next "ifconfig wlan0 up") */
+	kfree(fw);
+	fw = NULL;
+	fw_len = 0;
 	if (!session)
 		return -EIO;
 	memcpy(dev->dev_addr, mac, 6);
@@ -1353,6 +1358,8 @@ static int twl_write_proc(struct file *file, const char __user *buffer, unsigned
 		return -EFAULT;
 	cmd[n] = 0;
 	if (!strncmp(cmd, "clear", 5)) {
+		kfree(fw);
+		fw = NULL;
 		fw_len = 0;
 		return count;
 	}
